From 4ff860d36c81817731b1b82df355171f2c379a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:04:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/43] pvr: report real sampler limits (16 -> 32), probed not
 assumed

maxPerStageDescriptorSamplers / maxPerStageDescriptorSampledImages were 16 - the Vulkan
minimum, not the silicon's limit - and the per-set values were derived as 3*16. On this part
the vendor driver reports 32 per stage, and applications needing more than 16 samplers in a
stage refuse to run.

Probed with bench/pvr-vulkan/samplers: a 32/64/96/128-element sampler2D array where texture i
is a 1x1 image holding the value i and the shader writes each sampled value to slot i, so the
readback proves both the count and that every index reads the RIGHT texture (aliasing or a
short array would show wrong values, not zeros):

  NS=32   32 correct, 0 wrong
  NS=64   64 correct, 0 wrong
  NS=96   96 correct, 0 wrong
  NS=128 128 correct, 0 wrong

So at least 128 samplers work per stage and per set. Set to 32 per stage (vendor parity, well
inside what was probed) and 3*32 per set.

No regressions: bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize all still PASS; glmark2 --validate still 0
failures / 27 pass.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index 08e31c0..ca92d6c 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -752,19 +752,23 @@ static bool pvr_physical_device_get_properties(
       .bufferImageGranularity = 1U,
       .sparseAddressSpaceSize = 0U, /* Requires sparseBinding */
       .maxBoundDescriptorSets = 4U,
-      .maxPerStageDescriptorSamplers = 16,
+      /* Probing (bench/pvr-vulkan/samplers) shows 128 samplers in one stage and one
+       * set all sample their own correct texture - the limit was being reported as 16,
+       * the Vulkan minimum, which makes applications refuse to run. The vendor driver
+       * reports 32 on this part, so match that. */
+      .maxPerStageDescriptorSamplers = 32,
       .maxPerStageDescriptorUniformBuffers = 13,
       .maxPerStageDescriptorStorageBuffers = 16,
-      .maxPerStageDescriptorSampledImages = 16,
+      .maxPerStageDescriptorSampledImages = 32,
       .maxPerStageDescriptorStorageImages = 4,
       .maxPerStageDescriptorInputAttachments = 4,
       .maxPerStageResources = 57,
-      .maxDescriptorSetSamplers = 3U * 16U,
+      .maxDescriptorSetSamplers = 3U * 32U,
       .maxDescriptorSetUniformBuffers = 3U * 12U,
       .maxDescriptorSetUniformBuffersDynamic = 8U,
       .maxDescriptorSetStorageBuffers = 3U * 4U,
       .maxDescriptorSetStorageBuffersDynamic = 4U,
-      .maxDescriptorSetSampledImages = 3U * 16U,
+      .maxDescriptorSetSampledImages = 3U * 32U,
       .maxDescriptorSetStorageImages = 3U * 4U,
       .maxDescriptorSetInputAttachments = 4U,
 
